=== S. Theory (sympy) ===
S1 eps: d ln a0/dt = -3*H*(w + 1)/2  ; minus [-(3/2)H(1+w)] simplifies to 0
    CFG911 K17 form d ln a0/d ln a = -(3/2)(1+w): residual 0
    z-form: p = (1+z) rho'/3 - rho satisfies continuity (residual 0); -1/2 (1+z) H rho'/rho = -(3/2)H(1+w) (residual 0)
S2 -p: -p = -z*Derivative(rho(z), z)/3 + rho(z) - Derivative(rho(z), z)/3 ; d(-p)/dz = -z*Derivative(rho(z), (z, 2))/3 + 2*Derivative(rho(z), z)/3 - Derivative(rho(z), (z, 2))/3 ; residual vs (2/3)rho' - (1+z)rho''/3: 0
    fluid: d ln(-p)/dt = p_dot/p = 3H c_a^2 (1+w)/(-w): residual 0 => for -p > 0, rising <=> c_a^2 (1+w) > 0; with NEC (1+w>0) rising <=> c_a^2 > 0, falling <=> c_a^2 < 0
    rising -p in time <=> d(-p)/dz < 0 <=> (1+z) rho'' - 2 rho' > 0 : z*Derivative(rho(z), (z, 2)) - 2*Derivative(rho(z), z) + Derivative(rho(z), (z, 2)) > 0
    canonical scalar: d(-p)/dt = 2 V' phi_dot + 3 H phi_dot^2: residual 0
      slow-roll attractor (V' = -3H phi_dot): -3*H*pd**2  (< 0: -p falls);  flat potential V' = 0: 3*H*pd**2 (> 0: -p rises, NEC holds)
      scalar rho_dot = -3*H*Derivative(phi(t), t)**2 (= -3H phi_dot^2 <= 0 always: a canonical scalar's density never grows)
S3 V: V_dot = Derivative(V(phi(t)), phi(t))*Derivative(phi(t), t) ; d(phi_dot^2)/dt = -2*(3*H*Derivative(phi(t), t) + Derivative(V(phi(t)), phi(t)))*Derivative(phi(t), t) => V rises only while the field climbs (V' phi_dot > 0), and then phi_dot^2 must fall: transient, decelerating
    z-form: K = (1+z) rho'/6 (res 0), V = rho - (1+z) rho'/6 (res 0), V' = (5/6) rho' - (1+z) rho''/6 (res 0)
    no ghost <=> K >= 0 <=> rho' >= 0 ; rising V in time <=> (1+z) rho'' - 5 rho' > 0
S4 (TRUE BY CONSTRUCTION) inside a CFG689 segment rho = a + m z: d/dz of (eps, -p, V) = [m, 2*m/3, 5*m/6] -> all sign(m)
S5 IDENTITY (no verdict weight): S_dS/k_B = pi c^5/(G hbar H_L^2), H_L = Z a0/c, Z^2 = 32 pi/3 -> 3 c^7/(32 G hbar a0^2): residual 0 ; d ln S/dt = -2 d ln a0/dt
  [PASS] K4 sympy S1-S5 + CFG911 K17: all residuals zero

